    "reason": "The release note [ev-c24af5717093] is just a PR title. It doesn't say which flags are deprecated, what their new names are, or what happens when the old names are used. The linked PR [ev-8a7523f06d19] adds only a little: it fixes a logic issue with \"the webhook flag\", where both the deprecated and the new flag had to be disabled to turn it off. It doesn't name either flag, and it points to issue #6469 and PR #6427, which aren't shown here. The changed-files entry [ev-94966176064d] (cmd/crossplane/core/core.go) and the surrounding section don't fill these gaps. To write the assertion we still need the old and new flag names, the aliasing behaviour, and whether or when the old names will be removed.",
